url: "https://github.com/AlexKutepov/bartini-plus"
abstract: >-
  Open reconstruction of R. O. di Bartini's dimensional argument for n=6,
  analysis of 3+3 geometry, a stochastic extension (Bartini+) with P5 stress
  tests (Rubin monopoly bound, critical lock time, noise), field reduction
  via n in S^2 and Frobenius, theorems T1–T9 (including a no-go on mass
  from hidden times and Einstein-aether / GW170817 bounds), and M1–M3
  tightenings (maxent+Fourier, Dirichlet-to-c1 lemma, physical spectral
  dimension d_s=4). Numerical tests L0–L3. Hypothesis posed by Alexander
  Kutepov; mathematics and simulations produced jointly with LLMs. Does not
  claim a proof that the Universe is six-dimensional. See docs/*/FOR_RESEARCHERS.md.
